note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note tests/d8_process_tax.om -- developer bar D8, no per-process CUDA tax (docs/issues/D8-process-tax.md).
note Compiled by the pinned seeded omc (omega-mv e5b32567, sha256 2c82480596bbdc50cda9626866209ef662d5834f278f839ff4ce0250c495029f).
note Host forms checked with the omega lookup tool at that pin. It replaced tests/run_d8_process_tax.sh (CUDApp#366).
note   d8_process_tax dry-run OUTDIR HELLO HELLO_CONTROL        host only: no GPU, no lease; the GPU devices hidden
note   d8_process_tax gpu OUTDIR HELLO HELLO_CONTROL            GB10: one spark-window lease, three runs, judged
note   d8_process_tax check-gpu OUTDIR                         judges a recorded gpu run again; opens no device
note   d8_process_tax inside-window OUTDIR HELLO HELLO_CONTROL  only under spark-window run (the lease holds the chip)
note An empty OUTDIR selects build/d8-process-tax-dry-run (dry-run) or build/d8-process-tax/UTC-STAMP (gpu).
note HELLO and HELLO_CONTROL are build/hello_gpu and build/hello_gpu_control; make builds them first.
note Exit: 0 PASS, 1 FAIL, 2 NOT_RUN, 90 refused (arguments, a buffer bound or a failed host call).
note
note What is measured. hello_gpu prints its own overhead line (examples/hello_gpu/hello_gpu.c, D8): resident memory
note (VmRSS) before the GPU opens, after it opens and with its buffers allocated, its own buffer bytes, and what the
note session asked the driver for. With --hold-ms it prints its pid and holds its buffers; during the hold this program
note reads the same process from outside: VmRSS from /proc/PID/status and, on the GPU, the memory the driver reports for
note the pid (nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps, a read-only ORACLE). The measured process is build/hello_gpu itself.
note GPU runs, all in one lease, each a separate process:
note   main        hello_gpu --hold-ms=3000                                 must PASS the bar
note   n1-short    hello_gpu_control --bug=short --hold-ms=3000             negative control: must FAIL B1
note   n2-ballast  hello_gpu_control --d8-ballast-mib=512 --hold-ms=3000    negative control: the open cost must show the
note               512 MiB held across the open, and the run must FAIL B5
note The D8 verdict is PASS only when main passes AND both controls are caught.
note Dry run (host simulator, hello_gpu --sim, the same line without the open): the same three runs, a device-hidden
note run of the GPU path that must stop at NOT_RUN, the hold bound (--hold-ms=60001 refused with exit 2), the ballast
note flag refused by the default build (exit 2), and a self-test of the GPU judge and verdict on synthetic logs
note (labelled synthetic; they are not measurements). The dry run says nothing about the chip.
note
note The bar, registered before any chip run (2026-11-06, on CUDApp#280 commit 074adab1):
note B1 run      hello_gpu exits 0 and prints "checked 1048576 of 1048576 elements: 0 wrong, 0 never written" and PASS.
note B2 line     exactly one well-formed D8 line; its open cost and "beyond own buffers" equal the differences of the
note             numbers it prints; own buffers 12288 KiB (sim) or 12288..12352 KiB (a, b, c plus the code buffer).
note B3 outside  the hold line names the pid this program started, and VmRSS read from outside during the hold is within
note             4096 KiB of the line's "with buffers" number.
note B4 driver   (GPU) the driver's per-process report lists the pid with a whole number of MiB. Missing is FAIL.
note B5 tax      TAX = max(0, open cost, resident beyond own buffers) + max(0, driver MiB x 1024 - own buffers KiB)
note             (GPU) or max(0, resident beyond own buffers) (sim), and TAX <= 262144 KiB.
note 262144 KiB is 256 MiB (WolframLanguageEvaluator: 256*2^10 -> 262144); the pain D8 answers is about 4.6 GB per
note model: N[4.6*10^9/(256*2^20)] -> 17.136, the bar is 17.1 times below it. The ballast is 512 MiB
note (512*2^10 -> 524288 KiB the measurement must see).
note
note Host programs this driver starts, by absolute path: /usr/bin/bwrap (hides /dev/nvidia* for the dry run when the
note nodes exist), /usr/bin/nice and /usr/bin/taskset (D8_CORES pin, default 16,17; D8_CORES= runs unpinned), and on the
note gpu path /usr/bin/env, then spark-window, nvidia-smi, git and sha256sum found on PATH. execprog starts every child
note with an empty environment; spark-window needs HOME and PATH, so the gpu path passes HOME, PATH, USER, LOGNAME and
note SPARK_WINDOW_OWNER through /usr/bin/env until omega-mv has an execprog form that takes an environment.
note There is no signal-handler form at the pin either: an interrupted gpu run leaves its lease to expire (20 minutes).
note ---- storage (the shared part, regions and helpers, is tests/d8_lib.om). Regions here: 1 message, 4 OUTDIR,
note 5 this program, 6 HELLO, 7 HELLO_CONTROL, 10 outside pid, 11 outside VmRSS, 12 outside driver MiB, 13 hold pid,
note 14 failed bars, 15 lease id, 16 cores, 17 nvidia-smi, 18 spark-window, 20 child pid digits, 24 log path,
note 25 outside path, 26 file content, 27 verdict or lease path, 28 rc digits, 31 cwd and sha256sum.
global NV long 8
global J long 8
global E ulong 1
global PF uchar 8
global DE uchar 8192

